"Search the public web for pages such as documentation, articles, release notes and discussions. Returns numbered results with title, url, the published date when known, and a short excerpt. Each search costs money. Don't use it to find source code: it can't match exact identifiers, file paths, commit SHAs or a pinned version, and usually returns nothing useful for them. Read the code on disk, or use a code search tool, instead. Use include_domains to restrict to sites (bare hostnames such as example.com) and recency to limit results to recently published pages."
